namespace FamilyQuant;

public static class FamilyListImportHelp
{
    public const string Text = "IMPORT YOUR FAMILY LIST\n\n"
        + "1. Welcome. Choose an Excel workbook with an abbreviation and name for each family, or try the fictitious example. Save a template creates a reusable workbook. Edit current panel keeps the existing editor available.\n\n"
        + "2. File and sheet. Browse or drop one .xlsx file, choose its family sheet, and check the proposed header row. After editing the row number, press Read this header row. The preview retains source text and row numbers; select a cell and open Cell details for the complete text, fill name and merged range. Workbook colours are data, never decisions; yellow and gold fills are shown neutrally. Other sheets can be ignored or kept as original source notes.\n\n"
        + "3. Columns. Check each column choice and its example. Abbreviation and Family name are required. Other-language name, notes and Pfam are optional, and every original column is retained. Without a Decision column, every family is Quantify. If you choose a Decision column, review each distinct source value and its rows, edit its action or merge target, and press Confirm these actions. A colour category is optional; selecting it requires you to name each source colour.\n\n"
        + "4. Special rows. The source row, problem and proposed correction stay visible. Choose how to handle a row listing several names, a repeated abbreviation or a missing value, then press Use this choice. You may rename, skip or merge a repeated row; a several-name row can become one family per name or one group reported under others. Empty/decorative rows skipped by the reader remain listed. No unresolved row is silently dropped.\n\n"
        + "5. Evidence matches. Review suggestions from stored evidence, select the ones you want and confirm them, or skip that family. Counts are database entries per suggestion, not abundance; suggestions can overlap and must not be added together. No new suggestion is accepted by default. On re-import, previous confirmed choices are labelled Kept from previous panel; Keep previous matches retains their original values. Edited choices need explicit confirmation. Continue without matches skips new matching and leaves it for Panel checklist. The wizard never downloads evidence or assigns proteins.\n\n"
        + "6. Summary. Review the panel name, families, source notes, actions and matching choices. Import replaces the current panel, if any, as one project edit. Everything before Import is a detached draft; Back keeps your choices, and Cancel changes nothing. Source and project changes are checked again before publication.\n\n"
        + "7. Done. Open family checklist to review protein membership separately. Import itself leaves grouping and quantitation unchanged. Undo import restores the previous panel while this import remains the current Undo step. Close keeps the imported panel; File > Save persists it in the project.\n\n"
        + "KEYBOARD\nTab follows the controls in reading order; arrows work in native tables and choices. Enter activates the enabled forward action outside a table edit. Escape cancels or closes; F1 opens this Help.\n";
}
